<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juqu Anzhou</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 460</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juqu Anzhou was a prince of the Northern Liang, brother of its last ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juqu-mujian">Juqu Mujian</a>. After Northern Wei conquered Northern Liang in 439, he and his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juqu-wuhui">Juqu Wuhui</a> fled west and seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaochang">Gaochang</a> in 442. Around 450 Anzhou destroyed the kingdom of Jushi, and he ruled Gaochang until the Rouran killed him in 460.</p></div>
